{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":603,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:1Chr.6","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"1 Chronicles","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"1 Chronicles 6","reference":"1 Chronicles 6","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The first fathers of the tribe of Levi, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-3.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"The line of the priests from Aaron to the captivity, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"4-15.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"Of some other families, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"16-30.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"The work of the Levites, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"31-48 Of the priests, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":9,"text":"49-53.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":10,"text":"The cities of the priests and Levites, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":11,"text":"54- 81.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":12,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":13,"text":"The priest's office - So did all the rest, but it is implied that he did it worthily, he filled his place, and valiantly discharged his office in Uzziah's time.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":14,"text":"Solomon built - In Solomon's temple; so called to distinguish it from the second temple which was built or in building when these books were written.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":15,"text":"44.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":44,"scriptureVerseEnd":44},{"verse":16,"text":"Ethan - Called also Jeduthun, chap. ix, 16; 2 Chron. xxxv, 15, and in the titles of divers psalms.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":44,"scriptureVerseEnd":44},{"verse":17,"text":"54.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":54,"scriptureVerseEnd":54},{"verse":18,"text":"Castles - So called, not only because, walled and well guarded by the country; but because they and their possessions were in a particular manner the care of divine providence.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":54,"scriptureVerseEnd":54},{"verse":19,"text":"As God was their portion, so God was their protector.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":54,"scriptureVerseEnd":54},{"verse":20,"text":"And a cottage will be a castle to those that abide under the shadow of the Almighty.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":54,"scriptureVerseEnd":54},{"verse":21,"text":"The lot - Or, the first lot.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":54,"scriptureVerseEnd":54},{"verse":22,"text":"66.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":66,"scriptureVerseEnd":66},{"verse":23,"text":"Coasts - Or, of their borders, of their country contained within its borders.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":66,"scriptureVerseEnd":66}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":6}}